  "section_id": "s14-remember",
  "text": "Let's Remember. The Earth moves in two ways: rotation and revolution. Rotation causes day and night, while revolution causes seasons. The Earth completes one rotation in 24 hours and one revolution in three hundred and sixty-five and one quarter days. Solstices occur in June and December, marking the longest and shortest days. Equinoxes occur in March and September, when day and night are equal.",
